        <div id="dilution" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Dilution Ratios That Actually Matter
          </h2>

          <p>
            Every concentrate on this page is sold to be diluted, and the most common way to get poor results is to mix it the same way for every job. Too weak and the surfactant runs out before the oil does. Too strong and you waste money, leave a residue that attracts dirt and take twice as long to rinse. The right ratio depends on how much oil is on the surface and how long you can let it dwell.
          </p>

          <p>
            The makers' own numbers make the point. Zep lists its Driveway, Masonry and Concrete Cleaner at 6 ounces per gallon of hot water for light soil and 12 ounces per gallon for greasy concrete. Simple Green publishes Pro HD at 1 part to 3 parts water for heavy cleaning, 1 to 5 for medium and 1 to 10 for light. Oil Eater prints its dilution chart on the back label, with stronger mixes, down to equal parts water, for driveway oil and much weaker mixes, around 1 to 10, for general concrete floor cleaning. Retailer listings repeat different numbers for the same jugs, so treat the bottle in your hand as the authority.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Product</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Light soil</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Heavy soil</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Notes</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Zep ZUCON128</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">6 oz per gallon</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">12 oz per gallon</td>
